; Text in, one ASCII character a card, ended by -1, twice over (the host deals the text a second time); out the
; words, numbers and punctuation. The first time through it only looks for a small letter, and sends 1 if there is
; one (the text is not all capitals), else 0. The second time it asks the host for each character's row of the
; ASCII table (OUT at ask; its class and value come to INP at gc and gv): 1 a capital, 2 a small letter, 3 an
; apostrophe (part of a word); 4 a digit; 5 punctuation; 0 anything else. A word goes out as its letters' codes,
; then -10, then 1 if it has a small letter, else 0; a number as its digits, 500 + d, then -12; punctuation as its
; card (-2 to -5). Then -9.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            p1      INP   c        03-14: the first time: any small letter
  04                    CLA   c
  05                    TAC   p1e
  06                    SUB   c97
  07                    TAC   p1
  08                    SUB   c26
  09                    TAC   low
  10                    JMP   p1
  11            low     CLA   00
  12                    STO   lowt
  13                    JMP   p1
  14            p1e     OUT   lowt
  15            p2      INP   c        15-27: the second time: a character, and its class
  16                    CLA   c
  17                    TAC   fin
  18            ask     OUT   c
  19            gc      INP   cls
  20            gv      INP   val
  21                    CLA   cls
  22                    SUB   00
  23                    TAC   gap
  24                    SUB   n3
  25                    TAC   let
  26                    SUB   00
  27                    TAC   dig
  28                    JMP   close    28-32: punctuation: the token ends, the card goes out
  29                    OUT   val
  30                    JMP   p2
  31            gap     JMP   close
  32                    JMP   p2
  33            dig     CLA   mode     33-44: a digit: a word ends; the number goes on
  34                    SUB   n2
  35                    TAC   dg
  36                    JMP   dout
  37            dg      JMP   close
  38                    CLA   n2
  39                    STO   mode
  40            dout    CLA   val
  41                    ADD   c500
  42                    STO   x
  43                    OUT   x
  44                    JMP   p2
  45            let     CLA   mode     45-64: a letter or apostrophe: a number ends; the word goes on
  46                    SUB   00
  47                    TAC   ws
  48                    SUB   00
  49                    TAC   wout
  50                    JMP   close
  51            ws      CLA   00
  52                    STO   mode
  53                    CLA   z
  54                    STO   lw
  55            wout    OUT   val
  56                    CLA   cls
  57                    SUB   n2
  58                    TAC   p2
  59                    SUB   00
  60                    TAC   slw
  61                    JMP   p2
  62            slw     CLA   00
  63                    STO   lw
  64                    JMP   p2
  66            fin     JMP   close    66-68: the end
  67                    OUT   m9
  68                    HRS   00
  69            close   CLA   99       69-98: a word or a number ends
  70                    STO   ret
  71                    CLA   mode
  72                    SUB   00
  73                    TAC   ret
  74                    SUB   00
  75                    TAC   cw
  76                    OUT   m12
  77                    JMP   cz
  78            cw      OUT   m10
  79                    OUT   lw
  80            cz      CLA   z
  81                    STO   mode
  82            ret     DATA  0
  83            c       DATA  0
  84            cls     DATA  0
  85            val     DATA  0
  86            mode    DATA  0
  87            lw      DATA  0
  88            lowt    DATA  0
  89            x       DATA  0
  90            z       DATA  0
  91            n2      DATA  2
  92            n3      DATA  3
  93            c97     DATA  97
  94            c26     DATA  26
  95            c500    DATA  500
  96            m9      DATA  -9
  97            m10     DATA  -10
  98            m12     DATA  -12
